# ---- Book One ----
("Here is the thing almost nobody explains, and once you see it you cannot unsee it: **the spiritual realm runs on law, not on power.**",
 "*A note before this chapter: what follows uses a courtroom picture — legal ground, contracts, revoking — drawn from the legal language Scripture itself uses. It is a teaching frame, not a formula, and Christians hold different views on how literally to take it. Use what helps you, test all of it against Scripture, and never let it stand in for medical care, therapy, or safety.*\n\nHere is a picture that Scripture's own language makes possible: **the spiritual realm is not a contest of raw power. It is a matter of truth, law, and authority.**"),
("The Greek is *topos* — literally **place, ground, a legal foothold.**",
 "The Greek is *topos* — literally **a place, an opportunity, a foothold.**"),
("Sometimes a yes somebody else made on your behalf. It still functions.",
 "Sometimes a yes somebody else made on your behalf. It can still shape you."),
("The spirit realm recognizes **declared** agreement. That's why we renounce out loud — you are entering the same court the contract was filed in.",
 "Scripture takes spoken words seriously (Proverbs 18:21; Matthew 12:36–37; Romans 10:9–10). That's part of why we say these things out loud: speaking makes a decision real to *you*."),
("This isn't name-it-claim-it nonsense. It's that **you are a being with spiritual authority, and you used it against yourself.** That registers.",
 "This isn't name-it-claim-it nonsense, and your words did not seal your fate. But words shape how we see ourselves, and the ones you spoke in your worst hour have probably been echoing ever since. **You can bring them to God and speak something truer.**"),
("Sex is a **covenant instrument**, not a recreational act. It binds regardless of intent, context, or consent.",
 "Scripture treats sex as more than a casual act — it joins two people in a real way, which is part of why what happens there can leave a mark."),
("**Say the hard part out loud:** this includes what was done *to* you. A tie formed in assault is **not your sin** and it is **still a tie that needs cutting**. That's why a person you barely knew, or someone you never chose, can still have a hook in your body and your dreams twenty years later. You did not sign it. It still got filed. And it can still be cut.",
 "**Say the hard part out loud:** this includes what was done *to* you. What was done in assault is **not your sin** — it was a crime against you — and it can still leave a hold on your body, your dreams, and your trust twenty years later. You did not choose it, and you are not stuck with it. That kind of hold deserves real care: safe people, a trauma-informed counselor, and prayer."),
("**The thing nobody says:** a lot of survivors got into this **because nobody else was protecting them.**",
 "*Christians weigh some items on that list differently. Weigh them with Scripture and a trusted pastor. The point is not to frighten you about childhood games — it is to be honest about what you turned to for protection or answers.*\n\n**The thing nobody says:** a lot of survivors got into this **because nobody else was protecting them.**"),
("The word *pharmakeia* in Galatians 5:20 sits directly beside idolatry in Paul's list. Sit with that.",
 "Paul lists idolatry and sorcery (*pharmakeia*) side by side in Galatians 5:20. Scripture's concern is what rules you — not medicine taken under a doctor's care. If a prescription is part of your recovery, it stays."),
("unaddressed murder or abortion in the line", "unaddressed violence in the line"),
("Silence is the single most effective weapon against you, and it's the one your own family will help him enforce.",
 "Silence is one of the most effective weapons against you, and it's the one your own family may help enforce."),
("**This is why THKS exists. Saying it out loud is the warfare.**",
 "**This is why 7HE H0LY REUP exists. Saying it out loud is part of the fight.**"),
("**Every one of these was a child's attempt to build a father.** That's not wicked. It's grief.",
 "**Every one of these was an attempt to feel safe when nobody was keeping you safe.** That's not wicked. It's grief."),
("It functions like an open invitation, and it has to be revoked explicitly.",
 "It is not a spiritual contract you are trapped in. It is pain speaking, and it deserves a real answer: tell someone safe and get professional support."),
