# ---- Book Two ----
("A created being. An angel who fell (Isaiah 14:12–15; Ezekiel 28:12–17 — pride, self-exaltation, \"I will make myself like the Most High\"). Judged already. Sentenced already. Waiting for execution of sentence.",
 "A created being. Christian tradition reads Isaiah 14:12–15 and Ezekiel 28:12–17 (originally oracles against the kings of Babylon and Tyre) as also echoing the fall of a proud angel; the clearest New Testament glimpses are Luke 10:18 and Revelation 12:9. Either way: created, limited, already judged, waiting for the sentence to be carried out."),
("**He studies your patterns.** That's why patterns matter and why changing them blinds him.",
 "Scripture never says he can — though anyone who has watched a life for years can guess at patterns. That's one more reason to build healthier ones."),
("This is the one you asked for. Every stage, named. Read it and find yourself in it — and notice that seeing the plan on paper takes most of its power, because **every single stage depends on you not knowing it's a stage.**",
 "*A note before this chapter: this is a pattern-recognition tool, not a revealed schedule. Scripture says we are not to be ignorant of the enemy's designs (2 Corinthians 2:11), and it also says much of our trouble comes from our own hearts, other people, and a broken world. The stages are drawn from what Scripture warns about and from what survivors report. They are interpretation. Use them to notice patterns — never to decide that every hard thing in your life was a scripted attack, and never to blame yourself for what was done to you.*\n\nHere are twelve patterns that keep showing up in the lives of people who have been hurt and stuck. Read them and see where you recognize yourself — seeing a pattern on paper takes some of its power."),
("**This is where the generational curse gets renewed.** It doesn't automatically continue. **It continues because each generation re-signs it.**",
 "**This is where a family pattern gets passed on.** It doesn't automatically continue. **It continues when it goes unnamed and untreated — and it can stop when someone names it and gets help.**"),
("**Which is exactly why this workbook exists, and why THKS exists, and why you're going to open your mouth.**",
 "**Which is exactly why this book exists, and why 7HE H0LY REUP exists, and why you're going to open your mouth.**"),
("**Every single stage requires your unknowing cooperation.** Read that again. Not your consent — your **unknowing**. He needs you to not see the frame.",
 "**Every stage grows in secrecy and silence.** Read that again. Not because you failed — because being seen, known, and supported is what interrupts it. A pattern you can see is a pattern you can work on."),
("If you carry an assignment, the attack is not general. It's engineered. Here's the engineering.",
 "If you feel called to something, watch for these common ways a calling gets derailed. Some may be the enemy; many are simply human. You do not have to decide which in order to guard against them."),
("**Go back and look at what was attacked earliest and hardest. That's the blueprint he read before you did.**",
 "**Go back and look at what hurt earliest and hardest. That may point toward where you are meant to help — or it may simply be where you were hurt. Hold it loosely.**"),
("**Joseph got thirteen years first. That wasn't punishment — that was protection.**",
 "**Joseph got thirteen years first. Scripture doesn't say why, but it may have been preparation rather than punishment.**"),
("That's what THKS is — a building in the gap.", "That's what 7HE H0LY REUP is — a building in the gap."),
("**FAMILIAR SPIRITS** — the same thing, generation after generation, person after person. It knows your house.",
 "**FAMILIAR PATTERNS** — the same thing, generation after generation, person after person. Some believers understand this as a spiritual pattern; whatever you call it, it knows your house."),
("It is the single most reliable relapse predictor there is.", "It is one of the strongest relapse risks there is."),
("and he will time accusation to them.", "and accusation tends to hit harder at those times."),
("- [ ] Movement 20+ minutes daily — the only thing proven to move a craving in real time",
 "- [ ] Movement 20+ minutes daily — one of the best-supported ways to ease a craving in real time"),

