# ---- Book Seven: Brandi ----
("You built a movement because of a sister who didn't make it. You have said, out loud, that if a place like the one you're building had existed and she had reached for it, she might still be here.",
 "You built a movement because of a sister who didn't make it. You have said, out loud, that you wish she'd had a place like the one you're building — somewhere to reach when she knew something was wrong. No one can say whether it would have changed her outcome."),
("- **Part of the shape of your assignment.** Her absence is the exact shape of the thing you build — **a place to reach when you know something is wrong and don't know where to go.** That's the wound becoming a door. That's Joseph, starved of family, put in charge of feeding families.",
 "- **Part of why you build.** Her absence shapes the thing you are building — **a place to reach when you know something is wrong and don't know where to go.** That's a wound becoming a door, a little like Joseph, starved of family and later put in charge of feeding families."),
("**She knew. People in that condition often can't receive it, but not receiving it is not the same as not knowing it.**",
 "**I can't tell you what she knew. But love that was real does not vanish because it could not be received.** People in that condition often can't take it in, and that is not the same as it never mattering."),

# ---- Book Eight: two futures ----
("### Twenty years out, and the honest end of it\n\n**Here's the part nobody says out loud: for some people on this road, there is no twenty years.** Untreated addiction, untreated trauma, and untreated despair have a mortality rate. That's not a scare tactic, that's an obituary column. **You have read those names. You have buried one of them.**",
 "### Twenty years out, and the honest end of it\n\n**Here's the part nobody says out loud: untreated addiction, untreated trauma, and untreated despair do shorten lives.** That is not a scare tactic. It is why getting help matters. If that sentence is loud for you today, call or text 988 before you read another page."),
("The bridge she was supposed to build never got built, and the people who would have crossed it fell in the water, and they have names too, and she'll meet them one day.",
 "The bridge she was supposed to build never got built, and the people who would have crossed it went looking somewhere else."),
("Same woman. Same history. Same wounds. **Different terms.** Here is what actually happens, on a realistic timeline, because this part deserves detail too.",
 "Same woman. Same history. Same wounds. **Different choices.** Here is what *can* happen, on a realistic timeline, because this part deserves detail too. It is a picture of what is possible, not a promise."),
("They will grow up thinking the way you live is normal, and they will have no idea what it cost, and that is the definition of a curse being broken.",
 "They will grow up thinking the way you live is normal, and they will have no idea what it cost, and that is what a broken pattern looks like."),
("| **The contracts** | Still in force, still charging interest | Void, dated, nailed to the cross |",
 "| **The agreements made in pain** | Still running, still charging interest | Named, released, brought to the cross |"),

# ---- Book Nine ----
("Out loud matters — **the spirit realm responds to declared agreement, not private opinion.**",
 "Out loud helps — **saying it makes it real to you.**"),
("> I was consecrated before I was formed. The assignment came before the damage. The damage was aimed at the assignment — which means I know exactly where the treasure is buried, because I know where they dug.\n>\n> My wound is the shape of my assignment. I am the one who reaches back into the gap, because I have been in the gap, and I know the way out by name.",
 "> God knew me before I was formed, and what was done to me never canceled what He had in mind for me. The harm does not get the final word.\n>\n> My wound does not have to stay a wound. I can reach back into the gap, because I have been in the gap, and I know the way out by name."),
("> Every contract I signed in pain is void. Nailed to the cross. Dated and done.",
 "> Every agreement I made in pain, I bring to the cross, where the record of debt was nailed and canceled."),
("> The pattern that ran in my blood for four generations ends with me. I am the pivot. It does not pass to my children, and I have the date written down.",
 "> The pattern that ran in my family for generations can stop with me. I am choosing to be the pivot. I am working to keep it from passing to my children, and I have the date written down."),
("> What tried to end me is going to be the testimony that frees somebody else.",
 "> What tried to end me can become a testimony that helps somebody else."),
("**There is nothing in your life that the blood of Jesus Christ does not have legal authority over.**",
 "**There is nothing in your life that the blood of Jesus Christ does not reach.**"),
